From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ai_re <ai_re@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:10:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm: add an Annapurna Labs Alpine V3 target after al-boot
 stage3

U-Boot for Alpine V3 boards (16x Cortex-A72, "K2X"), started after
al-boot stage2/stage3 have trained DRAM, downloaded the SerDes firmware,
set up the lanes and installed the PSCI v0.2 monitor at EL3. No
low-level init, the same model as the Alpine V2 target (patch 0014) in a
board directory of its own (board/amazon/alpine-v3), so the V2 files stay
untouched:

- position independent, with a Linux Image header (text_offset = the
  link address, "place anywhere"), so it runs wherever it is loaded on a
  4 KiB boundary and the vendor U-Boot 2018.05 can start it with "booti"
  (in place), "bootm" of a kernel uImage, or "go";
- save_boot_params: "go" enters with the vendor MMU and caches on: clean
  the D-cache by set/way and turn them off before start.S continues;
  booti/bootm and stage3's agent arrive with them off. The entry EL, SCTLR
  and x0 are printed by checkboard();
- DRAM banks from /memory (CS8210: four banks, 9 GiB of address space for
  8 GiB); mem_map = DRAM as Normal, every hole below 4 GiB as Device
  (built after relocation from gd->dram);
- /reserved-memory ranges of the control DT keep ram_top (and so the
  relocated U-Boot) clear, and ft_board_setup() copies into the OS DTB's
  memory reserve map the ones its own /reserved-memory lacks;
- the architected timer runs from CNTFRQ_EL0, which the firmware sets
  (75 MHz on the CS8210, read from Linux userspace);
- load addresses for bootstd/boot.scr/extlinux/booti in the board env
  (the CS8210 NixOS bootmenu's layout), fdtfile from
  CONFIG_DEFAULT_FDT_FILE; initrd and FDT used in place;
- alpine-v3-u-boot.dtsi: bootph-all for the console path of the mainline
  alpine-v3.dtsi, for a board's -u-boot.dtsi to include.

Scope: alpine-v3.
